-- title:
--   Adic evaluation of a formal group law homomorphism at 0
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and $I \subseteq R$ an ideal such that $R$ is $I$-adically complete (separated and complete for the $I$-adic filtration). Let $F$ and $G$ be formal group laws over $R$, and let $\varphi$ be a homomorphism from $F$ to $G$ in the sense of the project's structure `LawHom`: a one-variable power series $\varphi.\mathrm{series} \in R[[X]]$ whose constant coefficient vanishes and which satisfies the compatibility $\varphi.\mathrm{series} \circ F = G(\varphi.\mathrm{series}(X_0), \varphi.\mathrm{series}(X_1))$, the left side being substitution of the two-variable series $F$ into $\varphi.\mathrm{series}$ and the right side substitution of the two series $\varphi.\mathrm{series}(X_i)$, $i \in \{0,1\}$, into $G$. The assertion is that the adic evaluation $\varphi.\mathrm{appAdic}\, I$, namely evaluation of $\varphi.\mathrm{series}$ on the $R$-algebra $R$ itself with respect to the $I$-adic topology, sends $0 \in R$ to $0$. Thus the point map attached to $\varphi$ on $I$-adic points fixes the origin.
--
--   This records that the map on $I$-adic points induced by a homomorphism of formal group laws is pointed, i.e. sends the zero point to the zero point, which is immediate from the vanishing of the constant coefficient. It is used in the proof that the maximal ideal of the universal deformation ring with Drinfeld level structure is generated by the two basis parameters ([`FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair_of_universal_of_isComm`](thm.html#FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair_of_universal_of_isComm)).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_FormalGroup_LawHom_appAdic_zero.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FormalGroup_NSeries
import Definitions.Def_FormalGroup_DrinfeldBasis
import Definitions.Def_FormalGroup_PointTransport

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open FormalGroup IsLocalRing

theorem FormalGroup.LawHom.appAdic_zero
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R) [IsAdicComplete I R]
    {F G : FormalGroup R} (φ : FormalGroup.LawHom F G) :
    φ.appAdic I (0 : R) = 0 := by sorry
